   106	  - Crater decouple proof holds: production config **holds** the poured crater; `center_pour_crater_slumps_without_blend` still slumps at blend 0. *(integration: bulk reduces to current)*
   107	  - **Covers R5 — main's drip-stir guard (telemetry + control).** Sustained *slow, sparse* drips onto a settled cup pool do NOT trigger spontaneous stir/blow-up: settled-tail KE bounded + non-growing + circulation bounded, under a long sustained-drip run. **Telemetry precondition:** particles crossing from air into the pool must measurably acquire **high `c`** (the merge discriminator is firing) — asserted *before* the KE/circulation bounds are deemed meaningful. **Mandatory control (same scene, same tuned curve, merge discriminator disabled → density-only keying):** MUST exhibit the stir — proving the merge guard prevents main's failure, not luck (mirrors the crater blend-0 negative control). *(error path: drip blow-up — the named main MPM failure mode)*
   108	  - **Covers R3 + transfer-side R1/R12.** Free-flight / post-cone water liveliness and surface velocity diversity rise materially vs the disabled (pure-PIC) baseline at a low cap-hit rate (mass-weighted, localized signal). **NOTE:** the *full pool-impact crown is NOT promised here* — a too-compressible pool still absorbs the drop until the deferred density-target pressure lands; this gate measures the **transfer-side** gain vs baseline, not absolute crown height. *(happy path: transfer-side liveliness — thresholds pinned after visual oracle)*
   109	- **Verification:** Visual oracle (live webapp, Debug Scenes catalog, twofield): free/impacting water shows a crown/scatter; settled pool stays calm; crater held. Then the quantitative signal above is pinned.
   110	- **Execution note:** Visual-oracle / measure-first — confirm the look and tune `c_surface`/thresholds before pinning numeric splash thresholds (no premature numeric gates).
