docs/plans/2026-06-06-006-feat-water-grain-coupling-physics-plan.md:226:**Approach:** Replace raw `fluid_impulse > wake_threshold` with a **dimensionless** wake gate (drag impulse relative to grain submerged weight, or sustained local relative-flow speed) so the threshold is independent of dt/subiters/neighbor count (KTD-9). Crucially the wake accumulator is **drag-only**: today `fluid_impulse` is written by both `drag_grain` and `buoyancy_grain` (coupling.wgsl:309, 353) — split it so **buoyancy does not contribute** (else a hydrostatic, zero-flow saturated bed wakes from buoyancy). Add explicit decay so a saturated, no-longer-flowing bed sleeps. Ensure `rolling_damping` doesn't fully cancel drag-driven surface motion. Dry bed (mixed gates off) untouched.
