docs/plans/2026-06-09-001-feat-unified-twofield-solver-plan.md:140:- **Approach:** Quadratic B-spline weights (KEEP.md §3 validated math), fixed-point `atomic<i32>` P2G scatter with documented FP_SCALE/velocity-cap headroom, per-particle affine C matrix carried and updated in G2P. Gravity on the grid, plus grid-node solid-boundary treatment against the scene SDF solids (separating/no-penetration condition on grid velocities, mirroring `src/utils/sdf.rs` conventions with a "mirrors utils::sdf" WGSL comment) — boundary handling is scoped work here, not an afterthought. No pressure yet — this unit's water is a momentum-correct splashing dust.
docs/plans/2026-06-09-001-feat-unified-twofield-solver-plan.md:143:- **Test scenarios:** free-fall matches the solver's own discrete recurrence within a documented float budget; P2G→G2P round trip conserves total mass and linear momentum exactly (fixed-point) for random particle sets; angular-momentum improvement of APIC vs PIC demonstrated on a rotating blob (discrimination gap asserted); fixed-point overflow probe at the velocity cap; particles settle on the container floor without wall penetration (grid boundary-condition gate); no NaNs across 1000 steps of a dam-break-shaped fall.
docs/plans/2026-06-09-001-feat-unified-twofield-solver-plan.md:170:### U5. Solid phase: stress, Drucker-Prager return map, compaction cap
docs/plans/2026-06-09-001-feat-unified-twofield-solver-plan.md:176:- **Approach:** Per-solid-particle deformation gradient F (or elastic strain in log space), 3×3 SVD in WGSL (port a verified branch-free routine; CPU twin mandatory), Klar 3-branch return map (elastic / yield-surface projection / tensile apex), friction angle from `Materials`, cohesion from `src/models/cohesion.rs` as a function of local saturation (dry in this rung), volumetric cap surface whose consolidation pressure ratchets with plastic compaction → packing fraction state per particle. Grid-level over-packing guard (the TFM solids-pressure pattern): φ_s is hard-clipped at the packing limit and a solids-pressure term that diverges as φ_s → φ_max resists further compaction in the two-field update — the particle-level return map alone cannot guarantee this on the grid. The guard enters the solid momentum equation as part of the effective/contact stress per KTD-5's partition — it is NOT a separate volume constraint and never appears in the projection; the U7 stress-partition audit verifies it is counted exactly once. Cost bound: solid counts are ~10–15k grains against 100k+ water, so the SVD/return-map is bounded; demoting it from per-substep to per-frame is a permitted knob ONLY if the repose/collapse gates are shown insensitive to the choice.
docs/plans/2026-06-09-001-feat-unified-twofield-solver-plan.md:193:- **Test scenarios:** drained flux through a static saturated column scales ∝ K(φ)·head and ∝ d² across a grind sweep (ordering + ratio bands); water entering the bed surface sees no pressure-jump barrier — entry flux matches the head-driven Darcy prediction within a stated band (the anti-divergence-penalty gate); drag pair update conserves combined momentum per node exactly; a settled saturated column stays settled long-run (drag does not pump energy); a submerged dense block in hydrostatic water exerts/receives the correct buoyant reaction — measured as the reaction impulse on the CONSTRAINED (frozen) solid equal to displaced-volume weight, since a frozen body has no dynamics to observe (dynamic buoyant motion is gated in U7); an undrained vertical load on a sealed saturated column transfers fully to pore pressure via the boundary reaction (the quantitative Skempton-B gate lives in U7 — a kinematically frozen skeleton has no volumetric strain path, so B is not meaningful here); the drag↔projection split is gated as a coupled system rather than assumed stable from the fold alone: under timestep refinement, slip-velocity decay matches the analytic exponential within a band with no oscillation growth and no energy increase (the partitioned-coupling gate at ρ_f/ρ_s ≈ 0.83); β-variation stress tests — high slip (nonlinear regime), dry→wet transition, φ near packing — show bounded error against a subcycled reference, where the reference subcycles drag AND projection together on a closed variable-φ two-phase column with outflow (the hard case is the full coupled loop, not drag decay in isolation); face-velocity consistency check — the velocities feeding D(φv) carry the same drag, pressure, solids-pressure, and boundary contributions as the momentum update (the multiphase Rhie-Chow corollary from KTD-2; a manufactured field where omitting any one term produces a detectable spurious φ_s oscillation); the U3 divergence-decay gate re-runs on a variable-φ saturated column against the mixture divergence (operator consistency in the φ<1 regime — the regime the novelty claim lives in); free-water region (φ_f = 1) behavior is byte-identical to U3 results (coupling terms vanish where there is no bed).
